<Project>

  <!--
    Copies licences/ into the build output, so the notices the product renders name files that are
    actually there.

    Three obligations land in that directory and none of them is satisfied by a link.

    The NVIDIA Open Model License covers the speaker diarisation weights, and §3.1 says a
    redistributor "must give any other recipients of the Model a copy of this Agreement". A copy,
    not a URL — and `uindosill notice` prints the path to it, so a build that leaves the file
    behind prints a promise it does not keep.

    ONNX Runtime is MIT, and MIT requires the copyright notice to travel with the binary. It also
    statically links 69 third-party components whose own notices are in its ThirdPartyNotices.txt,
    which is why that file is redistributed verbatim rather than summarised into the component
    table: summarising it would mean writing 69 licences by hand, and getting one wrong is the same
    breach as omitting it.

    Deliberately not conditional on a channel or a backend, unlike the CUDA runtime's notice. A
    notice that ships only when a flag says so is a notice that can go missing, and these are a few
    hundred kilobytes.

    The parakeet.cpp LICENSE is handled separately, by NativeAssets.targets: it travels beside the
    binary it covers, one per backend directory, so a drop that vendors only some backends still
    ships exactly the notices it needs.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../licences/*"
          Link="licences/%(Filename)%(Extension)"
          CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest"
          Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
